WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:06.190
Hello, everyone, and welcome to your second drink of The Duel.

2
00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:10.030
This might be one of my all-time favorite episodes of The Office.

3
00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:12.310
I know I say that so often.

4
00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:15.030
I also just really happen to like season five.

5
00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:17.190
Yeah, it's really solid.

6
00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:20.930
Well, there's just so many great moments in The Duel.

7
00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:24.190
I love the Andy and Dwight duel over Angela,

8
00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:27.810
but there's also all the scenes with Michael and David Wallace in New York.

9
00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:32.690
I'm very curious to hear what the fan favorite moment of this episode was.

10
00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:34.850
Well, we got this letter from Melissa Kay.

11
00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:36.050
Melissa says,

12
00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:36.790
Hi, ladies.

13
00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.330
Absolutely love your show.

14
00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:43.330
And one of my absolute favorite scenes from the whole show is at 10 minutes and 53 seconds

15
00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:47.550
when Michael is talking about his philosophy to David Wallace and says,

16
00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:53.730
Don't ever, for any reason, do anything to anyone for any reason.

17
00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:56.710
It goes on and on with this line.

18
00:00:56.710 --> 00:01:01.130
I love this line so much, and it completely captures the moment when you're asked a question

19
00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:04.030
you don't know the answer to, and you have to make it up as you go.

20
00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:07.190
Was all of that improvised, or was it fully scripted?

21
00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:08.150
Thanks, Melissa.

22
00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:11.010
Okay, so Melissa, we talked about this in our breakdown,

23
00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:14.910
how Steve improvised a lot of this, but we didn't play it.

24
00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:19.590
And I pulled a clip from the superfan version because there is an extra joke at the top,

25
00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:21.010
and it really cracked us up.

26
00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:22.450
Let's hear it.

27
00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:26.290
My philosophy is basically this.

28
00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:31.450
I like to sell paper for more than I bought the paper for.

29
00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:33.490
That's obviously obvious.

30
00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:36.810
But here's the thing, and this is something that I live by,

31
00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:39.510
and I always have, and I always will.

32
00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:48.970
Don't ever, for any reason, do anything to anyone, for any reason, ever,

33
00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:56.030
no matter what, no matter where, or who, or who you are with,

34
00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:09.040
or where you are going, or where you've been, ever, for any reason, whatsoever.

35
00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:12.120
Sometimes I'll start a sentence, and I don't even know where it's going.

36
00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:18.980
I just hope I find it along the way, like an improv conversation, an improvisation.

37
00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:24.540
I mean, it's something he lives by, and always will, for any reason.

38
00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.440
For any reason, for any reason.

39
00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:30.000
So not only was this our fan favorite moment of the episode,

40
00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:33.160
we also got a letter that this scene is educational.

41
00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.160
Listen to this.

42
00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:36.440
Angela B.

43
00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:37.680
wrote in and said,

44
00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:39.820
More of a comment for this episode.

45
00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:44.340
I taught English 101 at a university which focused on college writing.

46
00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:49.000
Every semester, whenever I did a lesson on needing to have a purpose for writing,

47
00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:54.340
I would show the clip from this episode where Michael starts to answer David Wallace's question

48
00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:58.520
and later says that he doesn't always know where his sentences are going to go.

49
00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:04.620
It's a great example about how if you don't know what the point of your argument or statement is,

50
00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:06.620
you'll end up with meandering thoughts.

51
00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:07.940
That's so wonderful.

52
00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:09.460
Hey, you know what?

53
00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:10.860
Just get it down on paper.

54
00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.060
You'll find it, right?

55
00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:18.360
Well, Angela, you might remember that I got really into the subject of dueling.

56
00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:24.300
When we did this episode, yes, I did a little deep dive on the rules of dueling.

57
00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:28.940
Well, we got some mail from folks that took my dive even deeper.

58
00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:31.860
And I'm going to read two letters that really tickled me.

59
00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:34.940
The first is from Laura H., who said,

60
00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:38.840
Hi, I really enjoyed the duel podcast episode.

61
00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:41.200
To add to your discussion of dueling,

62
00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:44.000
I wanted you to know that as an attorney in Kentucky,

63
00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:47.540
I had to be sworn in by the state Supreme Court.

64
00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:52.320
As part of the swearing-in process, attorneys have to solemnly swear,

65
00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:52.880
quote,

66
00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:56.600
that since the adoption of the present Constitution,

67
00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:59.440
I, being a citizen of this state,

68
00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:03.840
have not fought a duel with deadly weapons within this state,

69
00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:04.820
nor out of it,

70
00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:09.700
nor have I sent or accepted a challenge to fight a duel with deadly weapons,

71
00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:13.020
nor have I acted as a second in carrying a challenge,

72
00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:16.200
nor aided or assisted any person thus offending.

73
00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:18.520
Oh, my goodness.

74
00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:19.680
Laura said,

75
00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:23.940
The discussion regarding dueling is nearly half of the entire oath.

76
00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:25.980
That's bonkers.

77
00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:29.060
It was really funny to say that during the ceremony.

78
00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:30.900
And then Nicole C.

79
00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:31.880
wrote in to say,

80
00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:36.280
I enjoyed hearing your history of dueling and wanted to let you know something else.

81
00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:39.940
Yes, I am a lawyer in the military, a JAG.

82
00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:47.880
And the military has its own set of rules called the Uniform Code of Military Justice, or UCMJ.

83
00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:51.580
There is an article in the UCMJ, article 114,

84
00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:55.040
that makes it illegal for military members to duel,

85
00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:56.520
to promote a duel,

86
00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:59.260
to not take action in stopping a duel,

87
00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:01.800
or to fail to report a duel.

88
00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.420
So no dueling again.

89
00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:09.920
But then Nicole goes on to say that when we prepare to court-martial someone,

90
00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:13.480
they have models of the argument that they make.

91
00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:16.020
And Nicole said,

92
00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:18.840
If we were going to court-martial Andy for dueling,

93
00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:21.000
here is how that would be argued.

94
00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:22.200
Quote,

95
00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:25.020
In that Andy Bernard did,

96
00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:27.080
at or near the Scranton Business Park,

97
00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:28.600
on or about this date,

98
00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:30.600
fight a duel with Dwight Schrute,

99
00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:31.820
using as a weapon,

100
00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:32.300
therefore,

101
00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:33.780
a Toyota Prius.

102
00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:37.620
But Nicole says,

103
00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:41.180
There could also be a court-martial for Angela for promoting a duel,

104
00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:43.240
and it would sound like this.

105
00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:45.560
In that Angela Martin did,

106
00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:47.440
at or near the Scranton Business Park,

107
00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:48.660
on or about this date,

108
00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:51.140
promote a duel between Dwight Schrute and Andy Bernard

109
00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:53.300
by telling Andy he would be a coward

110
00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:56.280
if he failed to challenge Dwight to a duel.

111
00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:00.340
So, two sets of charges.

112
00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:01.720
I guess, though,

113
00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:03.700
maybe Dwight should be charged as well.

114
00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:04.560
He did participate.

115
00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:06.540
I found that all fascinating.

116
00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:07.400
I mean,

117
00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:10.220
people had a lot of thoughts on dueling.

118
00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:12.200
Dueling was like a big deal.

119
00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:13.100
Big deal.

120
00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:14.700
Well, listen, everyone.

121
00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:16.900
Thank you for tuning in.

122
00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:18.140
Thank you for writing in.

123
00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:19.960
Please write us your fan-favorite moments

124
00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:21.600
over in our second drinks folder

125
00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:23.320
at officeladies.com.

126
00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:25.300
And now, please enjoy the duel,

127
00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:26.420
but don't do a duel.

128
00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:27.000
No.

129
00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:30.040
And we've got really great tidbits in this one, too,

130
00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.360
from Jen Salata,

131
00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:32.320
director Dean Holland,

132
00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:33.700
and producer Randy Cordray,

133
00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:34.860
so go give it a listen.

134
00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:40.210
I'm Jenna Fisher.

135
00:06:40.390 --> 00:06:41.530
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

136
00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:42.770
We were on The Office together.

137
00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:44.050
And we're best friends.

138
00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:44.910
And now we're doing

139
00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:47.090
the Ultimate Office re-watch podcast

140
00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:47.870
just for you.

141
00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:48.490
Each week,

142
00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:50.350
we will break down an episode of The Office

143
00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:52.590
and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories

144
00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:54.190
that only two people who were there

145
00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:54.850
can tell you.

146
00:06:55.030 --> 00:06:55.990
We're The Office ladies.

147
00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:01.090
Lady, it's the duel.

148
00:07:01.490 --> 00:07:02.010
I mean,

149
00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:04.430
two men are gonna fight over me today.

150
00:07:05.890 --> 00:07:07.010
Me, a.k.a.

151
00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:07.970
Angela Martin.

152
00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:09.490
I have to say,

153
00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:11.270
like Andy's Prius,

154
00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:13.150
this episode sneaked up on me,

155
00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:14.930
but in a great way.

156
00:07:15.210 --> 00:07:16.190
Oh my gosh,

157
00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:16.770
Hidden Gem.

158
00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:18.130
It's so good.

159
00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:19.550
It's one of my favorite episodes.

160
00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:21.010
I loved watching it.

161
00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:22.150
I loved filming it.

162
00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:23.790
And I'm excited to talk about it today.

163
00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:24.370
Well,

164
00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:25.690
it is Season 5,

165
00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:26.730
Episode 12,

166
00:07:27.190 --> 00:07:28.590
written by Jen Salata

167
00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:30.190
and directed by Dean Holland.

168
00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:31.670
Here's your summary.

169
00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:33.530
Michael takes it upon himself

170
00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:35.830
to expose Angela and Dwight's affair

171
00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:36.570
to Andy.

172
00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:39.030
The two men then challenge one another

173
00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:40.870
to a duel in the parking lot.

174
00:07:41.090 --> 00:07:41.670
Meanwhile,

175
00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:43.790
Michael is summoned to corporate

176
00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:45.230
to speak with David Wallace.

177
00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:48.270
He thinks it's gonna be bad news,

178
00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:50.610
but he gets some unexpected praise.

179
00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:51.690
Oh,

180
00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:52.870
those scenes.

181
00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:53.810
We'll get to it,

182
00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:54.470
but man,

183
00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:55.390
those were good too.

184
00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:57.410
Fast fact number one,

185
00:07:57.630 --> 00:07:59.430
this episode was written

186
00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:00.790
